\ A raise from `(expected-close-paren)`, which `lib/pratt/arith.1z`'s `(parse-group)` calls in
\ tail position inside a `when` arm. The chain carries no `if` row for the `if` inside `when`.
\ That chain is the target every tier converges on.
\
\ Every tier renders it today only because the nested quotation's call resolves through the module
\ snapshot and stays interpreted. Routed through the captured-scope binding instead, the call
\ dispatches compiled and the chain gains the `if` row.
\
\ No flags: one golden binds the interpreted and eager suites. No AOT class builds
\ `lib/pratt/arith.1z` yet, so this file has no AOT twin. eager_tail_boundary_compiled_both.1z
\ reaches the same compiled-callee row without the library.

use "lexer" ;
use "pratt/arith" ;

TEST-LEXER: const ( -- lexer ) [
  V{ }
  skip-whitespace-rule #push!
  number-rule #push!
  { "+" "-" "*" "/" "(" ")" } symbols-rule #push!
  >array <lexer>
] ;

[ "(1 + 2" TEST-LEXER tokenize <arithmetic-pratt> parse-expr ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
